  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "A face that *goes white* has lost its color from fear or illness; many languages use the word for **pale** here, not the word for the color.",
    "grammar": null,
    "culture": "In many English-speaking countries **white** is the traditional color of a bride's wedding dress; in some other cultures white is the color worn when someone has died.",
